  "rationale": "TileLink is not an 8-bit byte-oriented command protocol. It is a 5-channel concurrent ready/valid protocol where 'commands' are encoded as multi-bit field tuples on each channel's opcode + param + size + source + address. Each channel has an independent opcode namespace; the same opcode value (e.g. 6) can carry different meanings on different channels.",
